craig@Vera:~/C_Programs/Console/cc_2/bin/Release$ ./cc_2 
Number:370000000000002
American Express
</code></pre>
<p>The key points to highlight are as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The sprintf function is utilized to convert an entered large integer value into a string, simplifying subsequent testing of the Luhn algorithm.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Odd/even digit summation is performed from the rightmost digit character to the leftmost character, again simplifying the summation and subsequent summation validity.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Having a character array for the credit card vendor check also can be simplified by treating each necessary character separately.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The major takeaway here would be to delve further into C tutorials regarding string and character functionality.</p>
